[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
Logstash 8 OSS was installed.

1) To start Logstash as an agent during system startup, run:

    sysrc logstash_enable="YES"

2) Extra options can be found in the startup script.

3) WARNING: In order for Logstash to work properly,
   procfs needs to be mounted on /proc.
   
   If you have not done it yet, please do the following:
   
           mount -t procfs proc /proc
   
   To make it permanent, you need the following lines in /etc/fstab:
   
           proc    /proc           procfs          rw      0       0
   
EOM
}
{ type: upgrade
  message: <<EOM
This package now uses the Apache-2.0 OSS distribution. X-Pack features,
including centralized pipeline management and X-Pack monitoring, are no
longer included. The elastic_integration filter is also omitted. Review
existing X-Pack settings and affected pipelines before upgrading.

Logstash 8.19.23 requires Java 21 by default. Review logstash_java_home in
/etc/rc.conf and any custom jvm.options before restarting the service.

The service now passes logstash_java_home and logstash_java_opts using
LS_JAVA_HOME and LS_JAVA_OPTS, as required by the upstream launcher.
Previously ignored settings will now take effect.
EOM
}
]
